      <div class="msv__alert msv__alert--red">
        <span class="msv__alert-icon">⚠️</span>
        <p><strong>Tax treaty gap — get professional advice:</strong> Without a comprehensive double tax treaty, South Africans face the risk of being taxed on the same income in both South Africa (where it originates) and Spain (where you reside). This is the single most important financial planning issue for South African NLV applicants. Consult a specialist in South African-Spanish cross-border taxation before committing to the move.</p>
      </div>
      <h3 style="margin-top: 1.5rem; margin-bottom: 1rem;">What this means in practice:</h3>
      <ul style="margin-bottom: 2rem;">
        <li><strong>Spanish tax residency:</strong> If you spend more than 183 days in Spain per year, you are a Spanish tax resident. Spain taxes your worldwide income — including South African pension annuities, investment income, and rental income from SA property.</li>
        <li><strong>South African tax residency rules:</strong> SARS (South African Revenue Service) uses a "ordinarily resident" test and the physical presence test. If you cease to be a South African tax resident (because you've permanently relocated), you may trigger an exit tax (deemed disposal of assets) on departure.</li>
        <li><strong>South African exit tax:</strong> When you cease to be a South African resident for tax purposes, SARS deems you to have disposed of your worldwide assets at market value. Capital gains tax may apply on unrealised gains — this can be a significant liability. Get tax advice before formally emigrating.</li>
        <li><strong>Pension annuity and living annuity income:</strong> These are taxable in South Africa at source (withholding tax applies). As a Spanish resident, Spain may also seek to tax this income — without a treaty, you may not receive full relief for the South African tax already paid.</li>
        <li><strong>SA financial emigration vs. NLV:</strong> Completing formal financial emigration from South Africa (ceasing SA tax residency) is a separate decision from obtaining the NLV. These two processes interact — you should plan both together with professional advisors.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

